# Cloudflare Pages redirects for the whole published site.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The site root served apps/home (the AI showcase
# homepage, dist/index.html) while the DOCS — the thing people come here for —
# sat a click away at /docs/. Landing on the docs is the intent, so the root
# now sends visitors there.
#
# WHY A REDIRECT RATHER THAN SERVING THE DOCS AT `/`. Moving apps/docs to
# base:'/' would collide with the Southleft marketing site. The docs app emits
# its scoped design-system pages under `southleft/` (dist/docs/southleft/...,
# served at /docs/southleft/), and apps/southleft publishes the MARKETING site
# to dist/southleft/ (astro.config.mjs base:'/southleft'). Rebase the docs to
# the root and both want /southleft/ — two different sites merging into one
# directory, with build:all's order silently deciding which files survive.
# Serving the docs at `/` therefore means relocating the marketing site first;
# it is not a one-line base change. It would also mean rebasing every docs
# asset path, the pagefind index (`pagefind --site ../../dist/docs`) and the
# gates that hardcode dist/docs (gate:docs-panels, check:coverage).
#
# NOTHING SERVES `/` ANY MORE. apps/home was dropped from build:all on
# 2026-08-27 ("i dont want to show it"), so no step writes dist/index.html and
# this redirect is the only thing answering the root. The app's source is still
# in the repo, parked and built by nothing -- see the "//build:app-home" note in
# the root package.json.
#
# IT WOULD WORK EITHER WAY. Cloudflare's rule is
# explicit: "Redirects are always followed, regardless of whether or not an
# asset matches the incoming request."
# (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/) -- so the rule fired
# even while dist/index.html still existed, which is how it was verified live
# before the homepage was dropped.
#
# `302`, NOT `301`, ON PURPOSE. A permanent redirect is cached hard by browsers
# and CDNs and is genuinely painful to walk back — anyone who loaded the root
# once keeps getting sent to /docs/ long after the rule changes. Keep it
# temporary until the docs-at-root question above is actually settled, then
# promote it.
#
# SCOPE: `/` matches the root path ONLY. A splat (`/*`) would capture the whole
# site, including /docs/ itself, and loop.
#
# HOW THIS REACHES THE ROOT. `pnpm run copy:pages-root` copies pages-root/ into
# dist/ during build:all, so this lands at dist/_redirects -- the same mechanism
# as _headers beside it. See pages-root/README.md.

/    /docs/    302
